      "side": 1,
      "message": ".weakKeys() is preferable here. Most keys are indeed reachable through the EffectiveModelContext, but not all. When the inference points at an rpc/action/notification, JsonParserStream gets its parent from DataSchemaCompat.toDataSchemaNode(), which returns a fresh OperationAsContainer/NotificationAsContainer every time (i.e. for every parseInput()/parseOutput()). With strong keys each such parse would leave an entry behind in the shared factory\u0027s cache. The weakKeys() drops them once the parser is gone. I can update the the comment to state it clearly.",
